y be the origin or compounding factor to a cough. Interestingly, one study in 1996 found that the character and\n[RAG context for 'She states she has had a cough for the past week' (score=0.83):]\n  Source: Hyperparathyroidism. > Complications\n  Neuropsychiatric manifestations, including fatigue, depression, anxiety, cognitive slowing, and muscle weakness, are common and may improve following parathyroidectomy, although evidence for this impr\n[Indirect reasoning chains (clinical inference):]\n  poorly controlled GERD with antacid use → calcium-containing antacid overuse → Gastrointestinal Medication-Related Hypercalcemia\n    (frequency: occasional)\n    Suggestion: Investigate the type of antacids used (e.g., calcium-based vs. magnesium-based) and measure serum calcium levels to determine if hypercalcemia is medication-induced\n  abdominal pain with unexplained weight loss → malignant neoplasm with PTHrP secretion → Solid Tumor-Induced Hypercalcemia via PTHrP Secretion\n    (frequency: rare)\n    Suggestion: Evaluate for occult solid tumors through imaging and PTHrP level measurement, especially if hypercalcemia is confirmed\n  abdominal pain + unexplained weight loss → metastatic cancer to bone → Metastatic Bone Disease from Solid Tumor\n    (frequency: occasional)\n    Suggestion: Perform bone imaging and tumor marker testing to assess for metastatic disease in the context of systemic symptoms\n\nWhen indirect_reasoning_chains are present, generate candidates that investigate the INTERMEDIATE phenotype to confirm or rule out the indirect association."}
